    {
      "id": "section:3/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "PM notifiers",
      "source_hash": 9295331990603436901,
      "context_hash": 10101036933491833489,
      "translation": "PM notifier",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "notifier": "notifier"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:23.215196Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Notifiers allow subsystems to react to suspend/resume events:",
      "source_hash": 9637676766101403903,
      "context_hash": 16178358694320092494,
      "translation": "notifier를 사용하면 서브시스템이 서스펜드/재개 이벤트에 대응할 수 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "notifier": "notifier",
        "subsystem": "서브시스템"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:23.215196Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Device suspend callbacks",
      "source_hash": 14484657431236876617,
      "context_hash": 14441838961490781160,
      "translation": "디바이스 서스펜드 콜백",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "callback": "콜백",
        "device": "디바이스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:23.215196Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The full driver PM callback sequence for system suspend:",
      "source_hash": 4644094401046620933,
      "context_hash": 4839590085096345317,
      "translation": "시스템 서스펜드를 위한 드라이버 PM 콜백의 전체 순서:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "callback": "콜백",
        "driver": "드라이버"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:23.215196Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "For most drivers, only `.suspend` and `.resume` need implementation.",
      "source_hash": 10628974496477350686,
      "context_hash": 14844150228520115199,
      "translation": "대부분의 드라이버는 `.suspend`와 `.resume`만 구현하면 됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "drivers": "드라이버"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:23.215196Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:3/seg:1",
      "source": "The `_noirq` and `_late/_early` variants are for hardware that requires very late/early access.",
      "source_hash": 10800972739033993381,
      "context_hash": 9851542900535233467,
      "translation": "`_noirq` 및 `_late/_early` 변형은 매우 늦은/이른 시점의 접근이 필요한 하드웨어를 위한 것입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "hardware": "하드웨어"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:23.215196Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "Minimal suspend implementation",
      "source_hash": 12153006937066158012,
      "context_hash": 7675776899069678212,
      "translation": "최소한의 suspend 구현",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774695Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Wakeup sources",
      "source_hash": 14367733292561542791,
      "context_hash": 4434018228742179066,
      "translation": "웨이크업 소스",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "A **wakeup source** is a hardware event that can wake the system from sleep.",
      "source_hash": 10464816428819800290,
      "context_hash": 6241974050368392895,
      "translation": "**웨이크업 소스**(wakeup source)는 시스템을 슬립 상태에서 깨울 수 있는 하드웨어 이벤트입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "hardware": "하드웨어"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Common wakeup sources: keyboard, touchpad, NIC (Wake-on-LAN), RTC alarm, USB.",
      "source_hash": 3416863266808978646,
      "context_hash": 7387389041150410552,
      "translation": "흔한 웨이크업 소스로는 키보드, 터치패드, NIC(Wake-on-LAN), RTC 알람, USB가 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "NIC": "NIC",
        "USB": "USB"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "Wakeup source tracking",
      "source_hash": 15546799789363606235,
      "context_hash": 11133152043111230244,
      "translation": "웨이크업 소스 추적",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Hibernate (suspend-to-disk)",
      "source_hash": 13877555674623621080,
      "context_hash": 3010634946211863713,
      "translation": "하이버네이트(suspend-to-disk)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Hibernation saves the entire memory image to disk, then powers off.",
      "source_hash": 9605405569840186538,
      "context_hash": 6336561640414761361,
      "translation": "하이버네이션은 전체 메모리 이미지를 디스크에 저장한 다음 전원을 끕니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "memory": "메모리"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "On resume, the image is read back and execution continues exactly where it left off.",
      "source_hash": 11762952830624237904,
      "context_hash": 12588346094734841811,
      "translation": "재개(resume) 시에는 이미지를 다시 읽어 들이고, 실행은 중단되었던 바로 그 지점에서 정확히 이어집니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "Hibernate state machine",
      "source_hash": 18396625108505900803,
      "context_hash": 17945885732958721756,
      "translation": "하이버네이트 상태 머신",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "state machine": "상태 머신"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "Configuring hibernate destination",
      "source_hash": 12244062622996787547,
      "context_hash": 15124865137778069005,
      "translation": "하이버네이트 저장 위치 설정",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Freeze (s2idle / S0ix)",
      "source_hash": 9491790727078586529,
      "context_hash": 3837809104493150860,
      "translation": "Freeze(s2idle / S0ix)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Modern laptops use **s2idle** (suspend-to-idle, sometimes called S0ix or \"connected standby\").",
      "source_hash": 10957501319841305034,
      "context_hash": 9797612198837926541,
      "translation": "최신 노트북은 **s2idle**(suspend-to-idle, S0ix 또는 \"connected standby\"라고도 함)을 사용합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Unlike S3, the CPU stays in a very shallow sleep state, allowing:",
      "source_hash": 18154121444328200582,
      "context_hash": 17883369122122758054,
      "translation": "S3와 달리 CPU가 매우 얕은 슬립 상태에 머무르므로 다음이 가능합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "Bluetooth/WiFi to stay connected",
      "source_hash": 11984472037046251662,
      "context_hash": 7544469072924710756,
      "translation": "Bluetooth/WiFi 연결 유지",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774696Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "Background tasks to run at reduced rate",
      "source_hash": 17501530413722102518,
      "context_hash": 9828586079471289523,
      "translation": "백그라운드 작업의 낮은 속도 실행",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:33.774697Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "Faster wake time than S3, since there's no full platform power-down/re-init to unwind — how much faster varies widely by platform and firmware",
